From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:06:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] downloads: fall back to copy+delete when SAF
 renameDocument is unsupported

ZhuoyiTong (HarmonyOS Android compatibility container) exposes a
DocumentsProvider that does not implement renameDocument(). Anikku
finalises every episode download by renaming "<episode>_tmp" to
"<episode>" with UniFile.renameTo(); on those devices the rename silently
fails, the episode stays in its _tmp directory and the download cache ends
up pointing at a directory that does not exist.

Add UniFile.renameToOrCopy(): try renameTo() first and, when it fails,
copy the file or directory tree to the destination and delete the source.
Devices whose provider supports rename keep the original code path.

While at it, create the .nomedia marker in the final episode directory
returned by renameToOrCopy() instead of the pre-rename handle.

Ported from Xun2202/mihon-harmony patch 0001 (based on zsyou/mihon-harmony;
upstream PR https://github.com/mihonapp/mihon/pull/3446).
---
 .../tachiyomi/data/download/Downloader.kt     |  5 +-
 .../core/common/storage/UniFileExtensions.kt  | 72 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

